<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39196" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιδια-βαίνω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>cross over after</i> another, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				4.122
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				6.70
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. τάφρον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					6.101
				</span></i>
			; [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποταμόν</span>] <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>HG</u>
				5.3.4
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. ἐπί τινα,
			τινί</span>, <i>cross a river</i> to attack an enemy, force
			the passage, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				3.14.8
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				2.5.8
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				D.C.
				60.21
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>. <i>pass
				all bounds</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταῖς ἐλπίσιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					J.
					<u>AJ</u>
					15.7.9
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>.
			<i>spread</i>, of diseases, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄχρι τῆς καρδίας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					8.297
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ γόνατα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aët.
					12.2
				</span></i>
			.</div>
